  "prompt": "HfFileSystem: \"x\"/\"xb\" writes with block_size=0 are silently dropped\n\nWith `block_size=0`, opening a file in exclusive-create mode accepts writes and closes without error, but nothing is uploaded:\n\n```python\nfrom huggingface_hub import HfFileSystem\n\nfs = HfFileSystem()\nwith fs.open(\"hf://datasets/<user>/<repo>/marker.txt\", \"xb\", block_size=0) as f:\n    f.write(b\"data\")   # returns 4, close() succeeds, no upload happens\n```\n\nThis also happens with text mode `\"x\"`, and when `block_size=0` is set on the instance (`HfFileSystem(block_size=0)`) and the open call doesn't override it. It affects repo and bucket paths. `\"wb\"` already raises a `ValueError`.\n\nThis is unlikely to be hit in practice, since it needs both streaming (`block_size=0`) and exclusive-create mode, but it's a silent data loss, so it's probably worth fixing anyway.\n\n**Cause:** `block_size=0` routes to `HfFileSystemStreamFile`. That class is read-only and inherits fsspec's no-op `_initiate_upload`/`_upload_chunk`. Its mode check rejects only modes that contain `\"w\"`. That was enough when the check was added (#1967). Then fsspec/filesystem_spec#1749 (fsspec 2024.12.0) made `\"xb\"` writable for `AbstractBufferedFile`. So on fsspec \u2265 2024.12.0, `\"xb\"` gets past the check and its writes go nowhere.\n\n**Proposed fix:** change the check to `mode != \"rb\"`. The error message stays the same. I've put the change and a regression test on a branch: https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface_hub/compare/main...davanstrien:huggingface_hub:hffs-stream-file-reject-write-modes. With fsspec 2026.9.0, the test fails on `main` for `\"xb\"`/`\"x\"` and passes with the fix. Read paths are unchanged, because fsspec normalises `\"r\"`/`\"rt\"` to `\"rb\"` before `_open`. Happy to open a PR if that helps, or feel free to take it.",
